<p class="copy">
	Only a handful of dreadnoughts exist in the settled systems, and every one is a unique engineering undertaking. The enormous expense involved in their design, construction, and upkeep makes them as much projects of national prestige as they are tools for protecting national interests. With tonnages in the millions and crews in the tens of thousands, these vessels are less ships than floating cities and pieces of national territory. Only the colossal <?php echo sf_lore_link('arks', 'Arks'); ?> exceed them in sheer scale, and a dreadnought is by far the most powerful warship one can encounter among the stars.
</p>
<p class="copy">
	Never deployed outside the center of a fleet, a dreadnought is always the command ship of whatever formation it belongs to. The weaponry of these vessels is as unique as the ships themselves, and each carries armor meters thick at its thinnest, with tens of meters of ablative and hard armor protecting its foresections. Despite, and perhaps because of, their sheer power, no dreadnought has ever engaged in full fleet-scale combat, and some have never fired their weapons in anger. Unsurprisingly, none has been lost in combat, and only one has ever been lost to accident: the infamous <i>Xù Rì</i> (Glorious, Rising Morning), which disappeared with all hands while transiting the stellar gulf between Sol and (Gl 15 A) Lóng gǎng (Dragon Harbor).
</p>
